<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elymians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Elymians were an ancient people of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> whose main towns were Segesta, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eryx">Eryx</a> and Entella. Greek writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> said they descended from Trojan refugees, and their language, known from short inscriptions, is still poorly understood. Often allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> against the Greek cities of Sicily, they were gradually Hellenised and absorbed into Roman Sicily.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elymians.jpg" alt="Elymians" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Halibutt · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sicily_prehellenic_topographic_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
